# Generated map layers -- rebuilt from the database on demand.
*.geojson
*.json
# The freshness sidecar has the same lifetime as the file it describes, and
# that file is ignored above. Committed, it would travel to a checkout where
# the geojson does not exist and claim it was current.
*.geojson.sig
# Terrain rasters, rebuilt by tools/build_terrain_overlay.py --dem.
# Tens of megabytes each and reproducible from USGS 3DEP, so they are
# generated, never committed.
*.png
# Baked aerial imagery, e.g. static/naip_teapot_wells.jpg from
# tools/build_terrain_overlay.py. Same reasoning as the terrain rasters
# above: 18 MB for the Teapot tile alone, and re-bakeable from NAIP, so
# it is generated on the machine that needs it, never carried in git.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
